de,{children:`unsafe-url`}),`.`]})}),_jsx(Warning,{children:_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(`b`,{children:`Programmatic access`}),` to logo images is not permitted and may result in\nrate limiting or blocking. Scraping logos will also lead to a block.`]})}),_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`If your use case requires caching, please `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://brandfetch.com/developers/contact/sales`,children:`contact us`}),` for a custom setup.`]})]}),_jsxs(Accordion,{title:`If you're an agent`,id:`if-you-re-an-agent`,children:[_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`A Logo API URL is for embedding, not for fetching.`}),` Requests that look programmatic are redirected to this page, with or without a client ID.`]}),_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Writing code or HTML that shows logos to a user?`}),` Put the URL in an `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\u003cimg>`}),` tag with the user’s client ID. `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://brandfetch.com/auth.md`,children:`brandfetch.com/auth.md`}),` explains how to get one: the user signs in at the developer portal and hands it to you.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Need the image bytes or brand data yourself?`}),` Don’t fetch the CDN. Use the `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/mcp/overview`,children:`MCP server`}),`, whose `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`get_brand_data`}),` tool returns credentialed asset URLs you can download, or the `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/brand-api/overview`,children:`Brand API`}),`. With no account, the Brand API can be `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/agents/pay-per-request`,children:`paid per request`}),`.`]}),`\n`]}),_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/agents/overview`,children:`Brandfetch for agents`}),` covers every way in.`]})]}),_jsxs(Accordion,{title:`Replicating Brandfetch`,id:`replicating-brandfetch`,children:[_jsx(_components.p,{children:_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`You cannot replicate the core user experience of Brandfetch.`})}),_jsx(_components.p,{children:`The best way to ensure that your application doesn’t violate this guideline is by integrating Brandfetch into an existing app that offers more value than just the Brandfetch integration.`}),_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Some examples:`}),_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`✅ The `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://brandfetch.com/developers/customers/typeform`,children:`Typeform integration`}),` improves the user’s onboarding by presenting brand logos. Without this integration, the app still has a lot of value to its users.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`✅ The `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://brandfetch.com/developers/customers/pitch`,children:`Pitch integration`}),` brings brand logos inside Pitch’s editor to streamline the creation of presentations. Without this integration, the app still has a lot of value to its users.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.li,{children:`🚫 A logo search that only returns logos from Logo API. Without the integration, the app has no content and no value to users.`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.li,{children:`🚫 An unofficial Logo API that allows users to access brand logos via Logo API. Without the API, the app has no content and no value to users.`}),`\n`]}),_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`If you’re unsure about your use case, please `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://brandfetch.com/developers/contact`,children:`contact us`}),`.`]})]})]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`rate-limits`,children:`Rate limits`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`We offer a fair use rate limit of `,_jsx(`b`,{children:`1,000,000 requests per month`}),` for free, which is designed to cover most small to medium applications, and paid plans include monthly volumes from 5 to 20 million requests — see the `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://brandfetch.com/developers/pricing`,children:`pricing page`}),`. These are soft limits and you won’t immediately be blocked if you exceed yours. Traffic that runs far beyond your allowance can eventually be refused with a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`429`}),` carrying `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#errors`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`quota_exceeded`})}),`.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`If your usage approaches your limit, we’ll send you a friendly heads-up so you can adjust your usage or explore an upgrade.`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`To maintain platform reliability, request throughput limits also apply:`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`1,000 requests every 5 minutes per IP`}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`2,400 requests every 5 minutes per customer`}),`\n`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Exceeding these throughput limits returns an HTTP 429 status code, without an `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`x-bf-error`}),` header. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#errors`,children:`Errors`}),` for how to tell a throughput block from the other reasons a request can be refused. Let us know if your application requires higher throughput.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`For enterprises, we provide custom solutions, including SLA agreements, custom terms, and flexible caching options to ensure optimal performance at scale. These plans are tailored to meet the needs of high-volume users.`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Feel free to `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://brandfetch.com/developers/contact/sales`,children:`contact us`}),` to discuss the right plan for your use case.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`errors`,children:`Errors`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`When the Logo CDN refuses a request, the response carries an `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`x-bf-error`}),` header naming the exact reason. A Logo API URL usually lives inside an `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\u003cimg>`}),` tag, where no response body ever reaches your page, so read that header in your browser’s network panel.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`403`}),` responses also return a JSON body with an `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`error`}),` code, a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`message`}),` written for a human, and a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`docs`}),` link. The other statuses are header-only. Some refusals are answered with a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`302`}),` redirect to our `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#usage-guidelines`,children:`usage guidelines`}),` instead of an error status; inside an `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\u003cimg>`}),` tag, that renders as a broken image.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Note,{children:_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`The throughput limits under `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#rate-limits`,children:`rate limits`}),` are enforced separately, so those responses carry no `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`x-bf-error`}),` header. The presence of the header is what tells you the CDN refused the request for one of the reasons below.`]})}),`\n`,_jsxs(Table,{children:[_jsx(_components.thead,{children:_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.th,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`x-bf-error`})}),_jsx(_components.th,{children:`Status`}),_jsx(_components.th,{children:`What happened`}),_jsx(_components.th,{children:`What to do`})]})}),_jsxs(_components.tbody,{children:[_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`client_id_invalid_signature`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`403`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`The `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`?c=`}),` client ID is present but doesn’t verify. This is almost always a transcription error.`]}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Copy the client ID from your `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://developers.brandfetch.com`,children:`developer dashboard`}),` instead of reading it off a screenshot. The message names the characters that get confused most often: lowercase `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`l`}),` against capital `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`I`}),` and the digit `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`1`}),`, and the digit `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`0`}),` against capital `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`O`}),`.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`client_id_disabled`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`403`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`The client ID has been disabled.`}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://brandfetch.com/developers/contact`,children:`Contact us`}),`.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`region_unavailable`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`403`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`The Logo CDN isn’t available in the viewer’s country.`}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Nothing you can change in the request.`})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`client_id_expired`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`410`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`The client ID carries an expiry that has passed.`}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Use a client ID from your `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://developers.brandfetch.com`,children:`developer dashboard`}),`.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`quota_exceeded`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`429`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Your organization has served far beyond its monthly Logo CDN allowance.`}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Raise your allowance and the block lifts within seconds. It also lifts on its own when your next billing period starts.`})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`rate_limited`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`429`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`The request was refused as abusive traffic.`}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Stop the source of the traffic, or `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://brandfetch.com/developers/contact`,children:`contact us`}),` if you believe your traffic was caught by mistake.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`client_id_required`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`302`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`The request carried no `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`?c=`}),` client ID. Every request needs one.`]}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Add `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`?c=YOUR_CLIENT_ID`}),` to the URL.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`user_agent_required`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`302`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`The request sent no `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`User-Agent`}),` header at all. This applies whether or not you send a client ID.`]}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Send a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`User-Agent`}),` header.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`hotlink_blocked`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`302`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`The `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`Referer`}),` is one we don’t serve logo traffic for, including `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`cdn.brandfetch.io`}),` itself.`]}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Embed the URL in your own pages with your own client ID, and check the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`Referrer-Policy`}),` requirements under `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#usage-guidelines`,children:`usage guidelines`}),`.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`automated_traffic`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`302`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`The request looks programmatic rather than a logo embedded in a page.`}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Embed the URL in an `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\u003cimg>`}),` tag. If your use case needs server-side access or caching, `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://brandfetch.com/developers/contact/sales`,children:`contact us`}),` for a custom setup.`]})]})]})]}),`\n`,_jsx(Warning,{children:_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`A valid client ID does not exempt a request from the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`automated_traffic`}),` check. A command-line fetch with a working client ID is still redirected, because Logo API URLs are meant to be embedded in your pages rather than fetched by a script.`]})}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`once-a-request-is-accepted`,children:`Once a request is accepted`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Anything past the checks above reaches the image itself. None of these responses carry an `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`x-bf-error`}),` header.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(Table,{children:[_jsx(_components.thead,{children:_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.th,{children:`Status`}),_jsx(_components.th,{children:`When`}),_jsx(_components.th,{children:`What you get`})]})}),_jsxs(_components.tbody,{children:[_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`200`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`A logo was found.`}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`The image, with `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ETag`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`Last-Modified`}),` headers. WebP unless you asked for another format.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`200`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`The brand is unknown, the identifier doesn’t resolve, the brand has no matching asset, or the URL itself can’t be parsed (for example a malformed domain such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`brandfetch..com`}),`).`]}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`A fallback image rather than an error status. Which one you get is set by the `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/logo-api/parameters#fallback`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`fallback`})}),` value in the URL.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`404`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`You asked for `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`fallback/404`}),` and no logo could be produced.`]}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`An empty body. The `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`404`}),` is cached for up to 7 days, so it can keep coming back for a while after a logo becomes available.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{\"data-numeric\":`true`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`503`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`A temporary failure on our side, not something your request caused.`}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Retry. There’s nothing to change in the request.`})]})]})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`There’s no `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`4xx`}),` for an unsupported `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`format`}),` or an out of range size either: an unrecognized `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`format`}),` falls back to WebP, a `,_jsx(_comp